Z||000005||Shaun41178||11-15-2001||02:10 PM||||DKOV, ITS NOT an Overhead cam!!!!!!  Its not even close!!!  <P>Quit giving false information.  That is why people on here can't keep their engines straight when one is mentioned because of false information that people like you give.<P>Pick up a book.  Its a pushrod engine.  Triad is talking about a 3.4 PUSHROD.  Not Overheadcam.<P>GM never made a 60 degree v6 single overhead cam engine (SOHC).<P>Come on man  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000006||DKOV||11-15-2001||03:33 PM||||My boo-boo... Don't boo-hoo  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The "push rod" motor is the smaller of the two... that is my point.  I have had the very same complaint about all the 3.4 motors getting tossed into the same basket.  I have started many a thread on WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT in reference to a statement regarding a 160 HP 3.4L motor.  My 3.4L is a TDC, also known as a DUAL overhead cam and base HP is 215.<P>RUMOR has it that there is such a thing as a SOHC, although I have never seen nor heard of one either.  I'm just repeating what I had read here on this forum.  I do know of a "push-rod" 3.4L and I had always assumed that the SOHC and the push-rod were the very same thing...<P>Until...<P>Someone, alot like you with your angry accusations, stringently corrected me saying the push-rod is a SOHC...<P>O well... do I really care?  Do I really want to put a 160 HP motor into my Fiero in the first place?  No, not really.  All I know for sure is that my 3.4L TDC motor is WAY TOO FAST and that suits me just fine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sorry if I offended anyone with a SOHC/push-rod (or whatever) motor out there.  I meant no harm.<P>So... don't EVER repeat anything posted on this forum... It MIGHT be wrong and you MIGHT get flamed....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
